# How to Update Styles Across Multiple Adobe InDesign Documents

Last updated: August 2026

Updating a style in one Adobe InDesign document is usually straightforward.

The problem becomes different when the same style changes need to be applied across a collection of InDesign documents.

A production project may contain dozens or hundreds of independent `.indd` files that are expected to follow the same style system.

This guide explains the practical ways to update styles across multiple InDesign documents, from Adobe's native workflows to batch processing for larger production collections.

