# Frequently Asked Questions

## How do I update a style across multiple InDesign documents?

For a small number of documents, styles can be edited or loaded using InDesign's native tools. For larger collections, especially independent documents that require the same repeated operation, a batch workflow can reduce manual work.

## Can InDesign synchronize styles across multiple documents?

Yes. InDesign provides native style loading and synchronization workflows. InDesign Books can also synchronize selected elements across Book documents.

## Can I use one InDesign document as a style reference?

Yes. A reference document can be used when loading or synchronizing styles.

## How do I rename styles across multiple InDesign documents?

For a small number of files, the operation can be performed manually. When the same renaming operation must be repeated across many documents, a batch workflow can automate the repetitive part of the process.

## Can Paragraph Styles, Character Styles, and Object Styles be renamed?

Batch Style Migrator supports renaming for all three.

## Can style properties be synchronized?

Batch Style Migrator can synchronize style properties from a reference document for matching styles.

## Can I preview changes before processing?

Yes. Batch Style Migrator includes a Simulation Mode.

## Does Batch Style Migrator support Style Groups?

Not in Version 1.0. Root-level styles are supported; styles inside Style Groups are currently ignored.

